From: taengu <7606218+taengu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:28:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Plugins: events go to their pages in batches

Each plugin event was its own emit, a script the page runs with the event
in its source, to every listening page. Loading into a zone sends
thousands: replaying a player's traffic in the KDE VM, the plugin
process went from 230 MB to 1.36 GB for those minutes. The flusher now
gathers a burst for 40 ms and sends each window one "plugin-events"
array, which the dock and plugin windows hand on one by one: the same
replay peaked at 376 MB.
